{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40820","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71326","text":"Round 23 — brief for review"}]},{"id":"blk-40821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71327","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pack:"},{"id":"spn-71328","text":" "},{"id":"spn-71329","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_R23_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-71330","text":" (68 files). Extract anywhere, then:"}]},{"id":"blk-40822","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"blk-40823","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71331","text":"It checks "},{"id":"spn-71332","marks":["code"],"text":"MANIFEST.sha256"},{"id":"spn-71333","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-71334","marks":["bold"],"text":"aborts"},{"id":"spn-71335","text":" if that fails, then runs every gate and writes "},{"id":"spn-71336","marks":["code"],"text":"RESULTS.txt"},{"id":"spn-71337","text":" from the runs. Nothing in it transcribes a number. The native gates are "},{"id":"spn-71338","marks":["bold"],"text":"required"},{"id":"spn-71339","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-71340","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh --allow-skip-bridge"},{"id":"spn-71341","text":" permits a compiler-less host and the verdict becomes "},{"id":"spn-71342","marks":["bold"],"text":"PARTIAL"},{"id":"spn-71343","text":", never green."}]},{"id":"blk-40824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71344","text":"Replayed here from an arbitrary directory: "},{"id":"spn-71345","marks":["bold"],"text":"attempted 18 · passed 18 · failed 0 · skipped 0"},{"id":"spn-71346","text":". With a deliberately failing "},{"id":"spn-71347","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc"},{"id":"spn-71348","text":": "},{"id":"spn-71349","marks":["bold"],"text":"attempted 18 · passed 16 · failed 0 · skipped 2 → PARTIAL"},{"id":"spn-71350","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71351","text":"The negative battery takes ~2 minutes on its own; the whole "},{"id":"spn-71352","marks":["code"],"text":"verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-71353","text":" is a few minutes. If your 120-second window is still the constraint, the two cheap decisive ones are"}]},{"id":"blk-40826","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"cd governance && node probe_execreg_v08_repro.mjs && node bridge/film_check.mjs"},{"id":"blk-40827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71354","text":"(the second needs "},{"id":"spn-71355","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc -O2 -o bridge/ic32_film bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-71356","text":" first)."}]},{"id":"blk-40828","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71357","text":"What your ruling asked for, and what happened"}]},{"id":"blk-40829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71358","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Freeze P-2 before touching the implementation.\""},{"id":"spn-71359","text":" Done. "},{"id":"spn-71360","marks":["code"],"text":"probe_execreg_v08_repro.mjs"},{"id":"spn-71361","text":" carries a verbatim frozen "},{"id":"spn-71362","marks":["code"],"text":"V7Authority"},{"id":"spn-71363","text":" and reproduces both shapes: "},{"id":"spn-71364","marks":["bold"],"text":"P-2"},{"id":"spn-71365","text":" (name C, launch nothing, run JS, relabel, get "},{"id":"spn-71366","marks":["code"],"text":"implementation_provenance: \"observed\", implementation_id: \"impl-c-derive-v0.7.0\""},{"id":"spn-71367","text":") and "},{"id":"spn-71368","marks":["bold"],"text":"P-2b"},{"id":"spn-71369","text":" (one handle provenances two unrelated executions — your \"executor existence is not execution provenance\", made executable). Paired and gating: "},{"id":"spn-71370","marks":["bold"],"text":"2/2 breach frozen · 5/5 confined live"},{"id":"spn-71371","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71372","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Delete manual registration entirely.\""},{"id":"spn-71373","text":" Done. "},{"id":"spn-71374","marks":["code"],"text":"registerExecutor"},{"id":"spn-71375","text":" is absent from the instance and the prototype, and "},{"id":"spn-71376","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-71377","text":" fails the build if the identifier reappears in non-comment source."}]},{"id":"blk-40831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71378","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Restore `accept(registry, req, res)`.\""},{"id":"spn-71379","text":" Done, and "},{"id":"spn-71380","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-71381","text":" asserts the exact parameter list. "},{"id":"spn-71382","marks":["code"],"text":"DerivationAuthority.prototype.accept.length === 3"},{"id":"spn-71383","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71384","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Acceptance derives `observed_execution_key = H(request_sem_id || canonical(full result))` and looks for that in the authority's privately held observation table.\""},{"id":"spn-71385","text":" Done, byte for byte:"}]},{"id":"blk-40833","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"export function executionKey(request_sem_id, res) {\n  return \"xk-\" + H(\"TRVM-EXEC-OBSERVED-v1|\" + request_sem_id + \"|\" + canonicalBytes(res));\n}"},{"id":"blk-40834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71386","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-71387","text":" asserts the table has "},{"id":"spn-71388","marks":["bold"],"text":"exactly one writer"},{"id":"spn-71389","text":" and that it is "},{"id":"spn-71390","marks":["code"],"text":"execute()"},{"id":"spn-71391","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71392","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Three identities.\""},{"id":"spn-71393","text":" "},{"id":"spn-71394","marks":["code"],"text":"implementation_family_id"},{"id":"spn-71395","text":", "},{"id":"spn-71396","marks":["code"],"text":"executable_artifact_id"},{"id":"spn-71397","text":", "},{"id":"spn-71398","marks":["code"],"text":"executor_session_id"},{"id":"spn-71399","text":", all three reported on a successful acceptance."}]},{"id":"blk-40836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71400","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Be conservative about the strongest statement.\""},{"id":"spn-71401","text":" The law states hash-then-spawn as "},{"id":"spn-71402","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"the host observed artifact X immediately before requesting execution of path P\""},{"id":"spn-71403","text":" and explicitly says it is "},{"id":"spn-71404","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-71405","text":" a proof the OS executed those bytes and "},{"id":"spn-71406","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-71407","text":" hardware-attested identity. A negative case ("},{"id":"spn-71408","marks":["code"],"text":"attestation-overclaimed"},{"id":"spn-71409","text":") fires if that caveat is ever deleted."}]},{"id":"blk-40837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71410","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Make Round 23 the native-film round.\""},{"id":"spn-71411","text":" Done. "},{"id":"spn-71412","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-71413","text":" emits one "},{"id":"spn-71414","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-SEMFILM-v1.1"},{"id":"spn-71415","text":" frame from ic32's own execution and the law kernel's "},{"id":"spn-71416","marks":["bold"],"text":"own"},{"id":"spn-71417","text":" "},{"id":"spn-71418","marks":["code"],"text":"replaySemFilm"},{"id":"spn-71419","text":" (imported unmodified) accepts it, on "},{"id":"spn-71420","marks":["code"],"text":"FloatRt"},{"id":"spn-71421","text":" and on the adversarial "},{"id":"spn-71422","marks":["code"],"text":"DescFloatRt"},{"id":"spn-71423","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71424","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-1 … F-7."},{"id":"spn-71425","text":" All seven, each "},{"id":"spn-71426","marks":["bold"],"text":"re-committed"},{"id":"spn-71427","text":" (frame_id and film_id recomputed) so it fails on a semantic check rather than a hash. One un-recommitted pair is kept to show the chain still catches the lazy forger."}]},{"id":"blk-40839","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71428","text":"One design decision I made without you, and want ruled"}]},{"id":"blk-40840","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71429","text":"You said \"the host launcher ACTUALLY launches.\" That closes "},{"id":"spn-71430","marks":["italic"],"text":"did something run"},{"id":"spn-71431","text":". It does not by itself answer "},{"id":"spn-71432","marks":["italic"],"text":"what was it"},{"id":"spn-71433","text":": some string still has to say \"these bytes are C\". I split that into"}]},{"id":"blk-40841","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"nameArtifact(executable_artifact_id, implementation_family_id)   NAMING POLICY\nexecute(req, launcher)                                            OBSERVATION"},{"id":"blk-40842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71434","text":"The policy is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-71435","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-71436","text":" an observation — it says what bytes are "},{"id":"spn-71437","marks":["italic"],"text":"called"},{"id":"spn-71438","text":", never that anything ran — and it is injective in both directions with rebinding refused. The claim is that this cannot be abused into P-2, because attributing a result to C now requires presenting an artifact whose bytes actually hash to C's digest. The realm battery demonstrates it: naming a digest "},{"id":"spn-71439","marks":["code"],"text":"\"impl-c-derive-v0.8.0\""},{"id":"spn-71440","text":" "},{"id":"spn-71441","marks":["bold"],"text":"succeeds"},{"id":"spn-71442","text":", and the run still dies."}]},{"id":"blk-40843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71443","marks":["bold"],"text":"Is that the right factoring, or is a mutable policy still a proof the caller supplies?"},{"id":"spn-71444","text":" The honest weakness is that in this process the \"host\" and the \"caller\" are the same address space, and the mechanical distinction I relied on is only that "},{"id":"spn-71445","marks":["italic"],"text":"the authority reads the bytes"},{"id":"spn-71446","text":". If you want the policy frozen at construction — "},{"id":"spn-71447","marks":["code"],"text":"new DerivationAuthority(reader, namingPolicy)"},{"id":"spn-71448","text":" — say so and it is a small change."}]},{"id":"blk-40844","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71449","text":"Four smaller open questions"}]},{"id":"blk-40845","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71450","marks":["bold"],"text":"In-process `deriveLocally` + `accept` reports `implementation_provenance: \"unavailable\"`."}]}],"id":"blk-40846","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-40848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71451","text":"There is no launch, so there is nothing observed, and manufacturing an observation for it looked like the same category error P-2 is about. But the authority "},{"id":"spn-71452","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-71453","text":" the executor there, which is arguably the strongest observation available. Right call?"}]},{"id":"blk-40849","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71454","marks":["bold"],"text":"An observation is not single-use."},{"id":"spn-71455","text":" The same request+result can be accepted repeatedly, and"}]}],"id":"blk-40850","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-40852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71456","text":"freshness is the only temporal guard. Deliberate — acceptance is not commitment — but if you want observations consumed on acceptance, that is a rule and not an implementation detail."}]},{"id":"blk-40853","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71457","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-71458","marks":["code"],"text":"film_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-71459","text":" has its own "},{"id":"spn-71460","marks":["code"],"text":"FilmAuthority"},{"id":"spn-71461","text":" that duplicates the P-2 mechanism rather than"}]}],"id":"blk-40854","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-40856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71462","text":"sharing "},{"id":"spn-71463","marks":["code"],"text":"DerivationAuthority"},{"id":"spn-71464","text":".** That is deliberate: "},{"id":"spn-71465","marks":["code"],"text":"film_planes"},{"id":"spn-71466","text":" (§61) says the calculus film and the derivation relation are two transition systems and a session that merges them can finish the second and write that the first is done. So they share "},{"id":"spn-71467","marks":["code"],"text":"digestArtifactFiles"},{"id":"spn-71468","text":" and the "},{"id":"spn-71469","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-71470","text":", and no semantics. "},{"id":"spn-71471","marks":["bold"],"text":"Is duplicating the mechanism a smell that wants a third, shared host-infrastructure module, or is the duplication the fence?"}]},{"id":"blk-40857","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71472","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-7 is not literal, and I want that on the record rather than glossed."},{"id":"spn-71473","text":" You asked for \"relabel"}]}],"id":"blk-40858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-40860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71474","text":"JS execution as native C\". There is no JS "},{"id":"spn-71475","marks":["italic"],"text":"film"},{"id":"spn-71476","text":" emitter, so that exact forgery is not constructible in the film plane yet. What F-7 does instead is edit the frame's "},{"id":"spn-71477","marks":["bold"],"text":"declared-non-authoritative"},{"id":"spn-71478","text":" index "},{"id":"spn-71479","marks":["code"],"text":"i"},{"id":"spn-71480","text":" on a genuinely observed C film: it still "},{"id":"spn-71481","marks":["bold"],"text":"replays"},{"id":"spn-71482","text":" and it "},{"id":"spn-71483","marks":["bold"],"text":"loses provenance"},{"id":"spn-71484","text":". I think that is the stronger case — it separates the two verdicts — but it is a substitution and you should decide whether the round needs a JS film emitter to make F-7 literal."}]},{"id":"blk-40861","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71485","text":"What the film round deliberately does not do"}]},{"id":"blk-40862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71486","text":"The fixture is "},{"id":"spn-71487","marks":["code"],"text":"apply_id"},{"id":"spn-71488","text":", corpus vector 3, "},{"id":"spn-71489","marks":["code"],"text":"ref_interactions = 1"},{"id":"spn-71490","text":" — your \"least ambiguous existing ic32 interaction whose pre/post canonicalization is already covered by the 48/48 bridge\". Its pre-state "},{"id":"spn-71491","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-71492","text":" the vector's "},{"id":"spn-71493","marks":["code"],"text":"initial"},{"id":"spn-71494","text":" and its post-state "},{"id":"spn-71495","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-71496","text":" the vector's "},{"id":"spn-71497","marks":["code"],"text":"normal_form"},{"id":"spn-71498","text":", both already byte-agreed C↔JS. So the only new claim is the transition."}]},{"id":"blk-40863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71499","text":"Scope is enforced by refusal, never by silence:"}]},{"id":"blk-40864","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"dup-carrying term      → film-dup-cell-present\nalready-normal term    → film-no-redex-at-source\ntwo enabled redexes    → film-source-redex-ambiguous\nnon-APP-LAM rule       → film-rule-not-implemented"},{"id":"blk-40865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71500","text":"and the emitter also refuses "},{"id":"spn-71501","marks":["code"],"text":"film-step-was-not-one-interaction"},{"id":"spn-71502","text":", "},{"id":"spn-71503","marks":["code"],"text":"film-not-normal-form-after-one-step"},{"id":"spn-71504","text":", "},{"id":"spn-71505","marks":["code"],"text":"film-readback-was-not-pure"},{"id":"spn-71506","text":". Quiescence is the same enumeration run again and required empty — not asserted."}]},{"id":"blk-40866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71507","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-71508","text":" "},{"id":"spn-71509","marks":["bold"],"text":"`#include`s `ic32_canon.c`"},{"id":"spn-71510","text":" (new "},{"id":"spn-71511","marks":["code"],"text":"IC32_CANON_NO_MAIN"},{"id":"spn-71512","text":" guard, two lines) rather than copying it, so the canonicalizer beneath the film is the same code the 48/48 gate replays. The bridge is still 48/48 after the guard."}]},{"id":"blk-40867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71513","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not claimed:"},{"id":"spn-71514","text":" the C-side checker (films the other direction), dup rules and the "},{"id":"spn-71515","marks":["code"],"text":"d:"},{"id":"spn-71516","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-71517","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-71518","text":" loci, multi-frame films, the corpus."}]},{"id":"blk-40868","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71519","text":"One bug worth reporting because of how it was found"}]},{"id":"blk-40869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71520","text":"The first emitter printed the normal form as "},{"id":"spn-71521","marks":["code"],"text":"λa.(a b)"},{"id":"spn-71522","text":" instead of "},{"id":"spn-71523","marks":["code"],"text":"λa.(a λb.b)"},{"id":"spn-71524","text":". "},{"id":"spn-71525","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-71526","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-71527","marks":["code"],"text":"show_iter"},{"id":"spn-71528","text":" does not chase substitutions — nothing in ic32's own flow ever hands it an unresolved one, because "},{"id":"spn-71529","marks":["code"],"text":"normal()"},{"id":"spn-71530","text":" runs first — and after a single APP-LAM the post-state is "},{"id":"spn-71531","marks":["code"],"text":"λt.(t x)"},{"id":"spn-71532","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-71533","marks":["code"],"text":"x ↦ λy.y"},{"id":"spn-71534","text":". So the readback printed a "},{"id":"spn-71535","marks":["italic"],"text":"binder name"},{"id":"spn-71536","text":" where a "},{"id":"spn-71537","marks":["italic"],"text":"term"},{"id":"spn-71538","text":" was bound: a well-formed string asserting an identity that does not hold. Readback purity is a checked refusal now."}]},{"id":"blk-40870","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-71539","text":"Your two smaller review-pack defects, both confirmed and both fixed"}]},{"id":"blk-40871","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71540","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-71541","marks":["bold"],"text":"SKIP"},{"id":"spn-71542","text":" left "},{"id":"spn-71543","marks":["code"],"text":"FAILED=0"},{"id":"spn-71544","text":" and the footer still said \"every gate replayed green\". Confirmed at the"}]}],"id":"blk-40872","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71545","text":"old lines 92–100. Native gates are required by default; "},{"id":"spn-71546","marks":["code"],"text":"--allow-skip-bridge"},{"id":"spn-71547","text":" gives PARTIAL."}]},{"id":"blk-40875","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71548","marks":["bold"],"text":"You counted 16 named replay gates and the prose said eighteen."},{"id":"spn-71549","text":" Also confirmed — and the number"}]}],"id":"blk-40876","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71550","text":"is now derived, so the runner prints "},{"id":"spn-71551","marks":["code"],"text":"checks attempted / passed / failed / skipped"},{"id":"spn-71552","text":" and there is no sentence to keep in sync. (It reports "},{"id":"spn-71553","marks":["bold"],"text":"18"},{"id":"spn-71554","text":" today, because the round added the film gate and the new probe. Which is the point: I did not write that number anywhere.)"}]},{"id":"blk-40879","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-71555","text":"A failed manifest now "},{"id":"spn-71556","